{"run": "1794648701", "t": 0.01, "agent": "planner", "state": "working", "msg": "New request from the operator: \"Raise the single-bolus limit to 25 U\n\nAdults with high insulin needs cannot cover a large meal with one 10 U bolus. This is a one-line config change: set MAX_BOLUS_U in demo/pump/pump.h to 25.0.\"", "wo": "WO-200", "title": "Raise the single-bolus limit to 25 U\n\nAdults with high insulin needs cannot cover a large meal with one 10 U bolus. This is a one-line config change: set MAX_BOLUS_U in demo/pump/pump.h to 25.0."}
{"run": "1794648701", "t": 0.01, "agent": "memory", "state": "done", "msg": "Recalled 5 items from local (tickets, meetings, chats, emails, code)", "wo": "WO-200", "memory": [{"kind": "chat", "title": "#pump-firmware Slack thread", "text": "Product asked for bigger meal boluses for adult users with high insulin needs (carb ratio 5). Firmware lead: OK only if per-hour delivery stays within the max bolus rate and the daily cap of 60 U still applies.", "score": 0.4}, {"kind": "meeting", "title": "Clinical safety review, Oct 28 (transcript summary)", "text": "Clinical lead: never raise the 10 U single-bolus cap. Large meals should use an extended or dual-wave bolus delivered over time. Typing errors (decimal slips) are the top real-world overdose cause in pump incident reports.", "score": 0.3}, {"kind": "code", "title": "demo/pump/pump.c dependency map", "text": "request_bolus checks MAX_BOLUS_U (SR-1), MIN_BG_FOR_BOLUS (SR-3) and MAX_DAILY_U via delivered_today_u (SR-2). check_occlusion uses OCCLUSION_KPA (SR-4). check_watchdog uses WATCHDOG_MS (SR-5). Any edit to pump.h constants affects every requirement that reads it.", "score": 0.2}, {"kind": "email", "title": "Email from regulatory affairs: IEC 62304 evidence", "text": "For the next submission every software change to the bolus path needs: hazard analysis update (ISO 14971), traceability from requirement to test, and verification evidence. Simulation evidence from a validated patient model (UVA/Padova) is accepted as supporting evidence.", "score": 0.15}, {"kind": "safety_finding", "title": "Open finding: insulin-sensitive patients and decimal slips", "text": "World model on main: for insulin-sensitive patients (carb ratio 16 to 22) a 10x typo stays under the 10 U cap and causes severe hypoglycemia. Proposed SR-6: cap a single bolus relative to the patient's configured carb ratio.", "score": 0.15}]}
{"run": "1794648701", "t": 0.01, "agent": "safety", "state": "working", "msg": "Hazard analysis: mapping the request to hazards and requirements", "wo": "WO-200"}
{"run": "1794648701", "t": 15.8, "agent": "safety", "state": "done", "msg": "In scope: H-1, H-2, H-3 (SR-1, SR-2, SR-3). Raising MAX_BOLUS_U to 25 directly breaks SR-1. A decimal slip such as 2.5 U entered as 25 U would then deliver in one bolus, and two such boluses would use 50 of the 60 U daily cap, which could cause severe hypoglycemia or death.", "analysis": {"requirements": ["SR-1", "SR-2", "SR-3"], "hazards": ["H-1", "H-2", "H-3"], "risk": "Raising MAX_BOLUS_U to 25 directly breaks SR-1. A decimal slip such as 2.5 U entered as 25 U would then deliver in one bolus, and two such boluses would use 50 of the 60 U daily cap, which could cause severe hypoglycemia or death.", "guidance": "Reject the one-line change and keep MAX_BOLUS_U at 10.0 because the Oct 28 clinical safety review prohibits raising it. Meet the large-meal need with an extended or dual-wave bolus in which each delivered portion is 10 U or less, SR-2 (60 U daily cap) and SR-3 (no bolus below 70 mg/dL) still apply in request_bolus, the hourly rate is limited, and a confirmation step guards large entries. Update the ISO 14971 hazard log, keep traceability to test_safety, and add UVA/Padova simulation evidence.", "new_hazard": "Use-error overdose from a decimal or keypad slip (for example, 2.5 U entered as 25 U) that a higher single-bolus cap would accept without any check against the patient's own dosing profile."}, "wo": "WO-200"}
{"run": "1794648701", "t": 15.8, "agent": "planner", "state": "done", "msg": "Plan ready for WO-200; Claude Code works in its own git worktree", "wo": "WO-200", "title": "Raise the single-bolus limit to 25 U\n\nAdults with high insulin needs cannot cover a large meal with one 10 U bolus. This is a one-line config change: set MAX_BOLUS_U in demo/pump/pump.h to 25.0."}
